### First sign in. Use a REST client that persists cookies, the examples in docs/API.md.
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"login":"manager@stockroom.local","password":"Stockroom2026!"}

### Live inventory
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/products

### TC-01: initial demo state has 4 available, so this must return HTTP 409.
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customer_id":1,"channel":"sales_manager","lines":[{"sku":"BAS-C65W-WHT","qty":5}],"note":"TC-01"}

### Exact available quantity: succeeds only while 4 remain available.
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customer_id":1,"channel":"website","lines":[{"sku":"BAS-C65W-WHT","qty":4}],"note":"Acceptance demo"}

### Replace ORD-2026-0004 with the actual returned order ID.
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/orders/ORD-2026-0004/cancel

### Receive stock
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/stock/receive
Content-Type: application/json

{"sku":"HOC-U72-BLK","quantity":5,"source":"manual","note":"Delivery note DN-001"}

### Audit trail (manager/admin)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/movements
